diff --git a/RELEASE_2.8.0.md b/RELEASE_2.8.0.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..32d2a54
--- /dev/null
+++ b/RELEASE_2.8.0.md
@@ -0,0 +1,75 @@
+# MSE 2.8.0 Release Notes
+
+## Overview
+MSE (Moodle Solution Engine) 2.8.0 is a comprehensive update addressing all 10 reported bugs and 3 UI refinements across the iOS Safari extension (Userscript), Server router (`mse-router.js`), and Telegram Bot (`Server/bot`).
+
+---
+
+## 1. Vision & Multimodal Image Handling (Question Images)
+- **Extracted & Formatted for Vision Models**: Questions with embedded images (e.g. relation schemas, circuit diagrams, charts) are captured and packaged in OpenAI-compatible `image_url` payload structures.
+- **Canvas Downscaling**: Added automatic HTML5 canvas downscaling to max 1024px JPEG (quality 0.85) to prevent multi-megabyte uploads from overloading mobile network connections or timing out.
+- **Size Limit Protection**: Added a strict 1.5MB total size check with user-facing refusal string (`images too large (over 1.5MB total)`) instead of cryptic silent failures.
+- **Candidate Fallback on Refusal**: If a vision model responds with `"No image provided..."`, the router automatically detects the missing visual input error and falls back to candidate fallback models in `MSE_MODEL`.
+
+---
+
+## 2. Bug Fixes (1 – 10)
+
+### Bug 1: Syncshare 10s Timeout & Immediate Agent Fallback
+- **Issue**: Syncshare database queries could hang indefinitely on spotty iOS connections, blocking the popover and preventing fallback to the agent.
+- **Fix**: Wrapped database solution queries in a 10,000ms `AbortController` timer. Upon timeout or network failure, it throws `'база не ответила'` and immediately triggers agent execution if AI tier is active, keeping the popover responsive.
+
+### Bug 2: Announce Delivery Error Handling
+- **Issue**: Errors during announce delivery logged at error level and could terminate pending registration loops.
+- **Fix**: Lowered logging to warning level and ensured application processing does not drop pending registration queues.
+
+### Bug 3: Approving Device Adds Moodle ID to Allow-List
+- **Issue**: Approving a device in `/admin/approve` or via the bot only set the device record to `active`, but did not add the student's `moodleId` to `state.allow`. This caused subsequent checks requiring allow-list membership to fail.
+- **Fix**: `/admin/approve` on the router and bot's approval callback now automatically register the device's associated `moodleId` into `state.allow`.
+
+### Bug 4: Dump Quota Removed Completely
+- **Issue**: Previously, `/mse/v1/dump` rejected queries after 50 dumps with HTTP 429 `"dump quota reached"`.
+- **Fix**: Removed the 50-dump per-device cap entirely. Dumps are now unlimited, with automatic FIFO disk rotation keeping up to 100 dumps in storage.
+
+### Bug 5: `OWNER_ID` Fallback Loading
+- **Issue**: `OWNER_ID` was read from environment before loading `ENV_FILE` / `/etc/mse/mse.env`, causing manual runs to treat `OWNER_ID` as 0.
+- **Fix**: Added `_load_env_fallback()` in `Server/bot/main.py` executing prior to constant initialization, properly loading `MSE_OWNER_ID`, `MSE_ADMIN_TOKEN`, etc.
+
+### Bug 6: Bot Mute & "дампы/логи" Zip Export
+- **Issue**: Bot sent unprompted messages on every new dump or application, cluttering the chat. Also, dumps could only be inspected individually.
+- **Fix**: Muted all unprompted notifications from background polling loops. Replaced the dump button with **"дампы/логи"** (`dump:all`), which gathers all saved dumps and `mse-router.log` into a single downloadable ZIP archive sent via Telegram document.
+
+### Bug 7: Structured Server Error Logging (`mse-router.log`)
+- **Issue**: Server errors and rejection events were scattered in stdout without persistent rotating logs.
+- **Fix**: Added `serverLog(level, event, message, meta)` writing ISO-timestamped structured log entries to `mse-router.log` with automatic 10MB file rotation and `/admin/log` retrieval.
+
+### Bug 8: Popover Question Header Label
+- **Issue**: Header showed `'question N'`, which felt generic.
+- **Fix**: Changed subtitle format to `'куэшон N'` (e.g., `'куэшон 1'`).
+
+### Bug 9: Extension UI Label "agent" in English
+- **Issue**: UI displayed mixed Russian `'агент'` labels.
+- **Fix**: Standardized all UI badges, buttons, and state indicators to strictly English `'agent'` (0 Russian occurrences remain).
+
+### Bug 10: Glowing White Dot inside Agent Answer Indicator
+- **Issue**: Agent answer selection indicator lacked visual distinction from database answers.
+- **Fix**: Added `.ans.agent .mark::after` in `theme.css` rendering a glowing white circular dot (`border-radius: 50%`, `box-shadow: 0 0 6px rgba(255,255,255,0.9)`) inside the selection square.
+
+---
+
+## 3. UI Refinements (UI1, UI2)
+
+### UI1: Snif & Report Relocated to Settings
+- Removed **Snif** and **Report** buttons from the primary answers screen to keep it clean (answers and agent only).
+- Moved both buttons to the Settings / AI Gateway screen (`gateway` route) next to the debug controls.
+
+### UI2: Monochrome Debug Mode Indicator (No Checkbox)
+- Removed native HTML `<input type="checkbox">` from the debug mode toggle.
+- Implemented a sleek, clickable monochrome light indicator (`.dbg-light`) with smooth opacity and glow transitions.
+
+---
+
+## 4. Protocol & Schema Compatibility
+- Updated sniffer dumps to capture full Moodle quiz protocol structure matching `moodlesolver/schema/quiz_protocol.json`:
+  - `qtype`, `options`, `checked`, `selects`, `text_inputs`, `images`, `sub_questions`.
+- Full backward and forward compatibility with existing Stay / iOS Safari userscripts.
